nue:** Management reaffirmed 2027 guidance of C$4.2B. Backlog is C$5.1B, about 1.2 times that figure. I found no 2026 base, so there is no growth rate.\n   - **Margins:** Operating margin should stay near 11%, flat on 2026.\n\n2. **Tarnwell Electric (TRNW), 11%:**\n   - **Revenue:** Expected to grow 6%, driven by price increases.\n   - **Margins:** Operating margin should rise to 14% from 12%, also on pricing. This is the strongest outlook of the five.\n\n3. **Braxen Cable (BRXC), 9%:**\n   - **Revenue:** About 2% growth. Volumes are flat, so the growth comes from passing cost increases through in pricing.\n   - **Margins:** Copper costs are up 18%, which squeezes margins. Earnings are expected to be flat, and no margin percentage was given.\n\n4. **Ostrand Meters (OSTM), 8%:**\n   - **Revenue:** A smart-meter contract with Norvane Utilities adds about 20% to 2027 revenue.\n   - **Margins:** Margins dip about one point as the Norvane rollout ramps. The source doesn't say whether this is operating or gross margin.\n\n5. **Kelby Switchgear (KLBS), 7%:**\n   - **Revenue:** Expected down 5%, as Kelby loses medium-voltage switchgear share to Tarnwell.\n   - **Margins:** Restructuring holds operating margin at 8%. This is the weakest outlook of the five.\n\nTaken together, Tarnwell and Ostrand have the clearest growth, Voltaris is steady, Braxen is flat, and Kelby is shrinking. Kelby's loss of share to Tarnwell is consistent with Tarnwell's growth.","ttft_ms":1713,"type":"result","duration_ms":33570,"uuid":"e7687c7b-b90b-44b7-8e57-03e457800ce6","ttft_stream_ms":1315,"time_to_request_ms":547,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":59,"system_prompt":33,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":71,"input_attachments":106,"input_hooks":13,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":41,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":36,"init_frame_send":23,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":9,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":4,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":42,"query_setup":10,"model